    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `rollout_return_step_indices`, the response does not say which step each kept latent belongs to, and `timesteps` is filtered along with the latents while `sigmas` stays `[T+1]`. Trainers index both by step number. `sglang-miles` already returns `latent_step_indices`; this brings it to main.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Record every timestep; only latents follow the filter, tagged with their original step in `RolloutDitTrajectory.latent_step_indices`.\n- Carry the field through the multi-output merge, the per-output select and the rollout API (missing in `concat` / `select` on `sglang-miles` too).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Filter `[1, 2, 3, 10]` vs unfiltered, same request: kept latents equal `full[:, idx]`; timesteps, sigmas and log-probs bitwise equal. Run on Qwen-Image (rollout API, n=2) and MiniMax H3 (DiffGenerator, n=1 and n=2, with the H3 rollout-controller follow-up stacked).\n- Unit tests updated; the new multi-output asserts fail without the `concat` / `select` change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39700940837](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39700940837)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39700940827](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39700940827)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39700940892](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39700940892)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
